chapter(3,'evs','celebrating-festivals','Celebrating Festivals',
 ("A festival of flowers","Rishi from Jammu is going on a bus to the Himalayas with his parents to visit his Mama, Mami and cousins Chiya and Nonikaa. On the way and at the village he sees hills covered with flowers, learns about tulips and the spring festivals of different places, and learns how to stay safe on the road."),
 [("The bus journey",["Rishi is travelling by bus with his parents to a small village near the mountains, where his Mama (mother's brother), Mami (Mama's wife) and his cousins Chiya and Nonikaa live.","He enjoys the bus ride. The roads have hairpin turns, the hills are covered with colourful flowers, and he can see tall trees far away.","On the road we see many signboards, such as No Parking, No Horn Please, Speed Breaker, No U-Turn, Men at Work and School Ahead. Each board gives a message that keeps us safe.","We should follow road signs and signals. We can draw and label signboards of our own, such as for the library, toilet, assembly, drinking water point, playground, stairs and our classroom."]),
  ("Reaching the village",["They get down at the bus stop near the village and Mamaji is there to receive them. They walk on a broad concrete road that later becomes a narrow mud road near the house.","At the gate Rishi sees a row of colourful flowers in the garden. He can name a rose, a marigold and a hibiscus, but he is amazed by one flower unlike any he has seen.","He asks his cousin Nonikaa the name of the flower, and she says it is a tulip.","Roads can be of different kinds: broad concrete roads, narrow mud roads, and winding hill roads. They change with the place."]),
  ("Lunch and the tulip festival",["Mami calls the children in for lunch. They eat a Kashmiri dish called haakh, a kind of leafy vegetable, with hot rice, and it is delicious.","Nonikaa says that there is a Kashmir tulip festival at this time of the year. A festival can celebrate a flower, a season or a good crop.","The food of different places is different. Haakh with rice is special to Kashmir, and we can ask our elders about the special food of our own place."]),
  ("Spring festivals in different places",["Rishi says that red flowers called buransh (rhododendron) bloom in spring in his place. On the spring festival there, people place mustard and buransh flowers at the doorstep of every home in the neighbourhood, and the elders bless the children and give them toffees and sweets.","Chiya says her friend Unni from Kerala celebrates Vishu at this time of the year. They use yellow amaltas flowers, fruits and vegetables to make Vishu Kani. Vishu Kani is an auspicious sight seen at sunrise on the first day of the Malayali new year, and it is supposed to bring a fruitful year.","Mami says spring is a celebration of nature. After the harsh winter the sun shines brightly, flowers bloom, the grass grows and the trees get new leaves.","In Jharkhand, people celebrate Sarhul in spring. They wear traditional clothes and walk in a procession to the sakhua tree with sakhua flowers and freshly germinated grains. They make offerings to the Earth and the Sun and sing and dance to drums such as the dhol and nagada."]),
  ("Seasons, food and clothes",["There are different seasons: spring, summer, monsoon and winter, and each has festivals of its own.","Each festival has special food, such as thekua for Chhath Puja, pitha for Bihu, plum cake for Christmas, gujiya for Holi, sadya for Onam, holige for Ugadi and seviyan for Eid-ul-Fitr.","We wear special clothes on festivals, and the clothes differ from place to place and from family to family.","Not everybody eats the same special food or wears new clothes on festivals, and we should be sensitive to everyone."]),
  ("Festivals bring us together",["Festivals bring families, friends and neighbours together. We meet relatives, share sweets, sing and dance.","When we celebrate with people of other places and communities we learn new customs, foods and songs.","Spring is a time of happiness. Children sing, 'Spring is in the air, happy children are everywhere'.","We can spend time in nature, in the mountains, near rivers and streams, and feel happy there."]),
  ("The Himalayas",["Gopu's and Rishi's stories take place in the north of India, where the most majestic mountains in the world lie.","These mountains are called the Himalayas, which means the 'home of snow'.","The highest peak in the world, Mount Everest, lies in our neighbouring country Nepal, and its height is about 8,848 metres."])],
 [("Match the food with its festival.",[("Read the festival names: Bihu, Chhath Puja, Christmas, Eid-ul-Fitr, Holi, Onam, Ugadi.","These are the festivals in the list."),("Match: Thekua with Chhath Puja, Pitha with Bihu, Plum cake with Christmas, Gujiya with Holi, Sadya with Onam, Holige with Ugadi, Seviyan with Eid-ul-Fitr.","Each festival has a special food linked to it."),("Check that each festival has been used once.","Every name is used once, so the match is complete.")]),
  ("Draw a signboard for the school library.",[("Decide the message: Silence, please, or Library.","A sign needs a short message."),("Choose a simple picture, like an open book, and bright colours.","Pictures are easy to understand quickly."),("Draw it on chart paper and explain it to the class.","Explaining checks that others can understand it.")])],
 ("Tell a friend about a spring festival, and the food and clothes on festivals, and why festivals are special.",["Spring is a season when flowers bloom and festivals like Sarhul and Vishu are celebrated","Each place and festival has special food and clothes","Festivals bring people together"],["Festivals are celebrated in the same way everywhere","Everyone eats the same food on festivals","Festivals are only for children"]),
 ["Spring is a celebration of nature when flowers bloom and new leaves come out.","Festivals are celebrated differently in different places, such as the Tulip festival, Vishu and Sarhul.","Each festival has special food and clothes.","Road signboards keep us safe when we travel.","Festivals bring families, friends and neighbours together.","The Himalayas are the 'home of snow' and Mount Everest, about 8,848 metres, is the highest peak."],
 [M("cf-1",1,"What is the flower that Nonikaa names as the Kashmir tulip festival flower?","Tulip",[("Rose","Rishi already knew the rose."),("Marigold","Rishi also knew the marigold."),("Hibiscus","Rishi knew hibiscus too; the new flower was the tulip.")],"The new flower in the garden was a tulip.",None),
  M("cf-2",1,"Which Kashmiri dish did the children eat with hot rice?","Haakh, a leafy vegetable",[("Gujiya","Gujiya is a sweet for Holi."),("Pitha","Pitha is a rice cake for Bihu."),("Plum cake","Plum cake is eaten at Christmas.")],"Haakh is a leafy vegetable eaten with rice in Kashmir.",None),
  M("cf-3",1,"What are the red spring flowers of Rishi's place called?","Buransh (rhododendron)",[("Tulip","Tulips are Kashmir's spring flowers in this story."),("Sakhua","Sakhua flowers are used at Sarhul."),("Amaltas","Amaltas flowers are yellow and used in Vishu.")],"Buransh, or rhododendron, are red spring flowers.",None),
  M("cf-4",1,"Which festival uses yellow amaltas flowers, fruits and vegetables?","Vishu",[("Sarhul","Sarhul uses sakhua flowers and grains."),("Holi","Holi is the festival of colours."),("Christmas","Christmas is celebrated in winter.")],"Vishu Kani uses yellow amaltas flowers, fruits and vegetables.",None),
  F("cf-5",1,"The highest peak of the world, Mount Everest, is in our neighbouring country Nepal.",True,"Mount Everest lies in Nepal and is about 8,848 metres high."),
  M("cf-6",2,"Which festival in Jharkhand is celebrated in spring?","Sarhul",[("Vishu","Vishu is from Kerala."),("Chhath Puja","Chhath Puja is not mentioned for spring in this chapter."),("Eid","Eid is a different festival.")],"Sarhul is a spring festival in Jharkhand.",None),
  M("cf-7",2,"What does the signboard 'No Horn Please' tell us?","Do not blow the horn here",[("Blow the horn loudly","The sign asks for silence."),("Park here","That is not its meaning."),("Turn back","That would be No U-Turn.")],"It asks us not to use the horn, for example near a hospital or school.",None),
  M("cf-8",2,"Which food goes with Chhath Puja?","Thekua",[("Plum cake","Plum cake is for Christmas."),("Sadya","Sadya is for Onam."),("Gujiya","Gujiya is for Holi.")],"Thekua is the special food of Chhath Puja.",None),
  S("cf-9",2,"The Himalayas mean the '____ of snow'.",["home","home of snow"],"The word Himalaya means the home of snow.",[("river","Himalaya means the home of snow, not river.")]),
  M("cf-10",3,"Why do many places celebrate spring with flowers?","Because after winter, flowers bloom and the weather is pleasant",[("Because flowers never grow in other seasons","Flowers grow in other seasons too."),("Because spring is the coldest season","Winter is the coldest."),("Because all festivals happen in spring","Festivals happen in all seasons.")],"Spring is a celebration of nature's new life.",None),
  F("cf-11",3,"Everyone celebrates every festival in the same way.",False,"Festivals are celebrated in different ways in different places."),
  M("cf-12",3,"Why are road signboards useful?","They tell us how to stay safe and follow rules",[("They are only for decoration","They give information and warnings."),("They are only for drivers","Walkers also follow signs."),("They are not needed","Without signs, roads can be unsafe.")],"Road signboards help everyone, drivers and walkers, to stay safe.",None)],
 svgs=[("c3-festivals-spring","A table of spring festivals from Kashmir, Jammu, Kerala and Jharkhand","Spring festivals of different places.")])
